Package: clusnalyst
Title: Point-and-Click Cluster Analysis of Molecular and Trait Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ebenezer", "Ogoe", , "ebenezerogoe@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = "Co-creator; wrote the 2026 package"),
    person("Michael", "Obeng", role = "aut",
           comment = "Co-creator of Clusnalyst (2022)"),
    person("Stephen", "Amoako", role = "aut",
           comment = "Co-creator of Clusnalyst (2022)")
  )
Description: A 'shiny' application and a set of plain R functions for
    clustering samples from dominant markers, SNP genotypes (CSV, VCF or
    HapMap), quantitative or mixed traits, and DNA or protein sequences.
    It computes distance matrices, builds trees by UPGMA, WPGMA, single,
    complete or Ward linkage, neighbour joining or BIONJ, and checks them
    with marker bootstrap support (Felsenstein 1985
    <doi:10.1111/j.1558-5646.1985.tb00420.x>), cophenetic correlation,
    average silhouette width, the gap statistic and Mantel tests. It also
    offers principal coordinates and principal components, k-means and
    partitioning around medoids, and exports a self-contained HTML report
    and an R script that reproduces the analysis.
